From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: rkvdec: Allow cache hints on the capture queue

A CPU that reads decoded pictures, to convert, scale or hash them,
reads them uncached: dma-contig allocates the capture queue coherent,
and mapping a 4K picture for the CPU takes about 14 ms on the RK3528.
Let userspace ask for non-coherent buffers with
V4L2_MEMORY_FLAG_NON_COHERENT; videobuf2 then syncs them for the CPU
when they are dequeued and for the device when they are queued.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 .../platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
index dd0f1b5..7899b68 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
@@ -1379,6 +1379,7 @@ static int rkvdec_queue_init(void *priv,
 
 	dst_vq->bidirectional = true;
 	dst_vq->mem_ops = &vb2_dma_contig_memops;
+	dst_vq->allow_cache_hints = 1;
 	dst_vq->dma_attrs = DMA_ATTR_ALLOC_SINGLE_PAGES |
 			    DMA_ATTR_NO_KERNEL_MAPPING;
 	dst_vq->type = V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE;
